{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,85p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs; sed -n '114,168p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs; sed -n '295,330p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs; sed -n '556,665p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs; sed -n '226,275p' ../agent-source/omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs\"","aggregated_output":"use core::time::Duration;\nuse std::marker::PhantomData;\n\nuse futures::channel::oneshot;\n\nuse omnipaxos::{\n    messages::Message,\n    storage::{Entry, Storage},\n    util::{LogEntry, NodeId},\n    ClusterConfig, OmniPaxos,\n};\n\nuse super::{\n    actor::{run, ActorConfig, ActorState},\n    event::{AppendError, Command, OmniPaxosEvent, RuntimeProposeErr},\n    traits::{ActorEntry, AsyncRuntime},\n};\n\n/// Configuration for the async runtime actor.\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct RuntimeConfig {\n    /// How often the actor calls `tick()` on the underlying OmniPaxos.\n    /// Should match the tick timeout budget used when building `ServerConfig`.\n    pub tick_period: Duration,\n    /// How often outgoing messages are drained and forwarded on the `outgoing_messages`\n    /// channel.\n    pub egress_period: Duration,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the actor's command channel.\n    pub cmd_channel_capacity: usize,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the outgoing message channel.\n    pub outgoing_capacity: usize,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the incoming message channel.\n    pub incoming_capacity: usize,\n    /// Bounded capacity for the event channel.\n    pub event_capacity: usize,\n    /// How long an `append_notify` call waits for its entry to be decided before\n    /// resolving with [`AppendError::Timeout`](super::AppendError::Timeout).\n    pub append_notify_timeout: Duration,\n    /// Bounded capacity for each per-subscriber decided-log stream returned by\n    /// [`OmniPaxosHandle::subscribe_decided`].\n    pub decided_channel_capacity: usize,\n    /// Maximum number of concurrently outstanding `append_notify` calls (i.e.\n    /// calls that have not yet resolved). Once reached, further `append_notify`\n    /// calls are rejected immediately with [`AppendError::TooManyOutstanding`]\n    /// rather than queued, so a stalled cluster (e.g. no leader) can't grow this\n    /// backlog without bound.\n    pub max_pending_appends: usize,\n    /// Maximum number of concurrent [`OmniPaxosHandle::subscribe_decided`]\n    /// subscribers. Once reached, a new subscription is rejected: the returned\n    /// receiver's channel is closed immediately without delivering any entries.\n    pub max_decided_subscribers: usize,\n    /// Fallback cap on how many outgoing messages the actor buffers internally\n    /// while waiting for room on the (bounded) `outgoing_messages` channel,\n    /// used only if that channel's own capacity can't be read. Past this cap,\n    /// the *oldest* buffered messages are dropped rather than growing without\n    /// bound -- safe because OmniPaxos already tolerates lost messages via its\n    /// own resend/retry mechanisms.\n    pub max_outgoing_buffered: usize,\n}\n\nimpl Default for RuntimeConfig {\n    fn default() -> Self {\n        Self {\n            tick_period: Duration::from_millis(10),\n            egress_period: Duration::from_millis(1),\n            cmd_channel_capacity: 1024,\n            outgoing_capacity: 10_000,\n            incoming_capacity: 10_000,\n            event_capacity: 1024,\n            append_notify_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5),\n            decided_channel_capacity: 1024,\n            max_pending_appends: 1024,\n            max_decided_subscribers: 128,\n            max_outgoing_buffered: 10_000,\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// A cloneable, `Send + Sync` handle to an OmniPaxos actor running in the background.\n///\n/// All state-mutating and read methods are `async`. Users must drive message transport\n/// externally via [`OmniPaxosHandle::outgoing_messages`] and\n/// [`OmniPaxosHandle::handle_incoming`]. Dropping every clone shuts the actor down.\npub struct OmniPaxosHandle<T>\nwhere\n    /// Append an entry and await its decided log index.\n    ///\n    /// Works from any node: the actor tags the entry with a unique id, routes it to\n    /// the current leader, and resolves the future when the assigned log index is\n    /// decided. If no leader is known yet, the call waits rather than failing fast --\n    /// it resolves once a leader is elected, or with `Timeout` if none is elected in\n    /// time. Fails with:\n    /// - [`AppendError::Timeout`] if the entry is not decided within\n    ///   [`RuntimeConfig::append_notify_timeout`] (including when no leader was ever\n    ///   elected in that time);\n    /// - [`AppendError::Propose`] if the underlying propose call itself failed (e.g. a\n    ///   reconfiguration is already pending) -- only when this node owns the pending\n    ///   call, otherwise it still resolves via `Timeout`;\n    /// - [`AppendError::Superseded`] if a leader change occurred before decision --\n    ///   a heuristic, not a certainty; see its doc comment for why, and check the\n    ///   returned index yourself if you need to know for sure;\n    /// - [`AppendError::TooManyOutstanding`] if [`RuntimeConfig::max_pending_appends`]\n    ///   outstanding calls are already queued.\n    ///\n    /// Uses [`RuntimeConfig::append_notify_timeout`] as the deadline; use\n    /// [`Self::append_notify_with_timeout`] to override it for a single call.\n    pub async fn append_notify(&self, entry: T) -> Result<usize, AppendError<T>> {\n        self.append_notify_inner(entry, None).await\n    }\n\n    /// Same as [`append_notify`](Self::append_notify), but `timeout` overrides\n    /// [`RuntimeConfig::append_notify_timeout`] for this call only -- e.g. to give a\n    /// latency-sensitive caller a shorter deadline, or a bulk/background caller a\n    /// longer one, without changing the default for every other call.\n    pub async fn append_notify_with_timeout(\n        &self,\n        entry: T,\n        timeout: Duration,\n    ) -> Result<usize, AppendError<T>> {\n        self.append_notify_inner(entry, Some(timeout)).await\n    }\n\n    async fn append_notify_inner(\n        &self,\n        entry: T,\n        timeout: Option<Duration>,\n    ) -> Result<usize, AppendError<T>> {\n        let (tx, rx) = oneshot::channel();\n        self.cmd_tx\n            .send(Command::AppendNotify {\n                entry,\n                timeout,\n                reply: tx,\n            })\n            .await\n            .map_err(|_| AppendError::Shutdown)?;\n        rx.await.unwrap_or(Err(AppendError::Shutdown))\n    }\n\n    /// Append an entry without waiting for decision. Mirrors the sync API.\npub fn spawn_actor<T, B, R>(op: OmniPaxos<T, B>, cfg: RuntimeConfig) -> OmniPaxosHandle<T>\nwhere\n    T: ActorEntry,\n    B: Storage<T> + Send + 'static,\n    R: AsyncRuntime,\n{\n    let (cmd_tx, cmd_rx) = async_channel::bounded(cfg.cmd_channel_capacity);\n    let (outgoing_tx, outgoing_rx) = async_channel::bounded(cfg.outgoing_capacity);\n    let (incoming_tx, incoming_rx) = async_channel::bounded(cfg.incoming_capacity);\n    let (event_tx, events_rx) = async_channel::bounded(cfg.event_capacity);\n\n    let state = ActorState::new(\n        op,\n        cmd_rx,\n        incoming_rx,\n        outgoing_tx,\n        event_tx,\n        ActorConfig::from(&cfg),\n    );\n\n    R::spawn(run::<T, B, R>(state, PhantomData::<fn() -> R>));\n\n    OmniPaxosHandle {\n        cmd_tx,\n        events_rx,\n        outgoing_rx,\n        incoming_tx,\n        decided_channel_capacity: cfg.decided_channel_capacity,\n    }\n}\n    /// that may have silently added to the shared batch buffer (a forwarded\n    /// proposal, an incoming replication batch, a reconfiguration stopsign),\n    /// pushes a `TrackIntent::Untracked` placeholder in `unconfirmed_local`\n    /// for each newly-added entry, keeping its FIFO count accurate.\n    ///\n    /// Growth is `(accepted_after - accepted_before) + (batched_after -\n    /// batched_before)`, computed with signed arithmetic and clamped at 0:\n    /// `accepted_idx` can legitimately *decrease* when a follower's log is\n    /// truncated by an incoming `AcceptSync` from a new leader, which isn't a\n    /// case with anything new to track.\n    fn track_batch_growth(&mut self, batched_before: usize, accepted_before: usize) {\n        let batched_after = self.op.get_batched_len();\n        let accepted_after = self.op.get_accepted_idx();\n        let added = accepted_after as isize - accepted_before as isize + batched_after as isize\n            - batched_before as isize;\n        let ballot = self.op.get_promise();\n        for _ in 0..added.max(0) {\n            self.unconfirmed_local\n                .push_back((TrackIntent::Untracked, ballot));\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Delivers an incoming `SequencePaxos`/BLE message to the core, tracking\n    /// any entries it silently adds to the shared batch buffer -- see\n    /// `track_batch_growth`.\n    fn handle_incoming_tracked(&mut self, m: Message<T>) {\n        let batched_before = self.op.get_batched_len();\n        let accepted_before = self.op.get_accepted_idx();\n        self.op.handle_incoming(m);\n        self.track_batch_growth(batched_before, accepted_before);\n    }\n\n    async fn handle_command(&mut self, cmd: Command<T>) {\n        match cmd {\n            Command::Append { entry, reply } => {\n                // Via append_tracked (not self.op.append) so a deferred write\n                // still gets its unconfirmed_local placeholder, keeping FIFO\n                // position exact for any append_notify entries batched alongside it.\n                let res = self\n                    .append_tracked(TrackIntent::Untracked, entry)\n                    .map(|_| ());\n                let _ = reply.send(res);\n            }\n            Command::AppendNotify {\n                entry,\n                timeout,\n                reply,\n            } => {\n                if self.pending.len() >= self.config.max_pending_appends {\n                    let _ = reply.send(Err(AppendError::TooManyOutstanding));\n                    return;\n                }\n                let id = EntryId(uuid::Uuid::new_v4());\n                let timeout = timeout.unwrap_or(self.config.append_notify_timeout);\n                self.pending.push_back(Pending {\n                    id,\n                    undispatched: Some(entry),\n                    assigned: None,\n                    deadline: Instant::now() + timeout,\n                    reply,\n                });\n                self.try_dispatch_undispatched();\n            }\n            Command::CurrentLeader { reply } => {\n                let _ = reply.send(self.op.get_current_leader());\n            }\n            Command::DecidedIdx { reply } => {\n                let _ = reply.send(self.op.get_decided_idx());\n            }\n            Command::ReadDecidedSuffix { from, reply } => {\n                let _ = reply.send(self.op.read_decided_suffix(from));\n            }\n            Command::SubscribeDecided { from, tx } => {\n                if self.decided_subscribers.len() >= self.config.max_decided_subscribers {\n                    // Reject: drop `tx` without storing it, closing the\n                    // subscriber's channel immediately with no entries delivered.\n                    return;\n                }\n                let mut sub = DecidedSub { next_idx: from, tx };\n                // Immediate catch-up: push whatever is already decided from `from`.\n                if Self::push_to_sub(&mut self.op, &mut sub) {\n                    self.decided_subscribers.push(sub);\n                }\n            }\n            Command::Reconfigure {\n                new_configuration,\n                metadata,\n                reply,\n            } => {\n                // Wrapped like handle_incoming_tracked: a stopsign accepted as\n                // leader is itself an untracked addition to the shared batch buffer.\n                let batched_before = self.op.get_batched_len();\n                let accepted_before = self.op.get_accepted_idx();\n                let res = self.op.reconfigure(new_configuration, metadata);\n                self.track_batch_growth(batched_before, accepted_before);\n                let _ = reply.send(res);\n            }\n            Command::TryBecomeLeader => {\n                self.op.try_become_leader();\n            }\n            Command::Reconnected { pid } => {\n                self.op.reconnected(pid);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// Drives the actor. Runs until all handles are dropped (both `cmd_tx` and\n/// `incoming_tx` senders closed).\npub(crate) async fn run<T, B, R>(mut state: ActorState<T, B>, _rt: PhantomData<fn() -> R>)\n    fn outgoing_buf_cap(&self) -> usize {\n        self.outgoing_tx\n            .capacity()\n            .unwrap_or(self.config.max_outgoing_buffered)\n    }\n\n    /// Non-blocking drain of `outgoing_buf` onto `outgoing_tx`. Uses `try_send`\n    /// so a merely-full channel (slow consumer) doesn't block the actor loop;\n    /// unsent messages stay in `outgoing_buf` (in order) for the next attempt.\n    /// If the buffer exceeds [`Self::outgoing_buf_cap`], oldest messages are\n    /// dropped — see [`RuntimeConfig::max_outgoing_buffered`].\n    fn drain_outgoing_buf(&mut self) {\n        let cap = self.outgoing_buf_cap();\n        trim_oldest(&mut self.outgoing_buf, cap);\n\n        let pending = std::mem::take(&mut self.outgoing_buf);\n        let mut iter = pending.into_iter();\n        for msg in iter.by_ref() {\n            match self.outgoing_tx.try_send(msg) {\n                Ok(()) => {}\n                Err(async_channel::TrySendError::Full(msg)) => {\n                    self.outgoing_buf.push(msg);\n                    break;\n                }\n                Err(async_channel::TrySendError::Closed(_)) => {\n                    // Receiver dropped — user is not draining outgoing. Discard\n                    // everything remaining; nothing left to retry against.\n                    return;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        self.outgoing_buf.extend(iter);\n    }\n\n    /// Enqueue one outgoing message without awaiting. Appends behind any\n    /// already-buffered messages (preserves order), then tries to drain.\n    /// Used for both core protocol traffic (via [`Self::flush_outgoing`]) and\n    /// runtime control-plane messages (`TaggedProposal` / `Assigned`).\n    fn enqueue_outgoing(&mut self, msg: Message<T>) {\n        self.outgoing_buf.push(msg);\n        self.drain_outgoing_buf();\n    }\n\n    /// Pull newly-produced OmniPaxos/BLE messages into `outgoing_buf` and drain.\n    fn flush_outgoing(&mut self) {\n        self.op.take_outgoing_messages(&mut self.outgoing_buf);\n        self.drain_outgoing_buf();\n    }\n\n    /// Push newly-decided entries to a single, freshly-added subscriber. Used\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The snapshot finding is now confirmed in scope. The async runtime has another concrete question: its completion loop checks whether an assigned index is decided before checking whether the assignment’s ballot was superseded. The API promises notification for the submitted entry, so I’ll investigate whether a replacement entry can occupy that index and cause a false success.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > runtime_candidate_build.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));m=json.load(open(r['audit_spec_path']));m['version']=r['audit_spec_version']\n# Controller-derived indexes are omitted in submitted map products.\nfor a in m['activities']:a.pop('behavior_ids',None)\nfor f in m['facts']:\n f.pop('established_by',None);f.pop('consumed_by',None)\nsources=[dict(id='M-runtime-notify',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs',start_line=53,end_line=221,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-runtime-assign',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs',start_line=335,end_line=551,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-runtime-loop',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs',start_line=556,end_line=709,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-runtime-handle',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs',start_line=114,end_line=164,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-runtime-errors',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/event.rs',start_line=34,end_line=77,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-runtime-config',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs',start_line=19,end_line=81,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-runtime-egress',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs',start_line=226,end_line=273,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-runtime-spawn',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/handle.rs',start_line=282,end_line=325,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-runtime-traits',file='omnipaxos_runtime/src/traits.rs',start_line=28,end_line=46,kind='interface_statement')]\nb1=dict(id='B-runtime-assignment',primary_activity='A7',execution_owner='ActorState command/runtime-message handling',protocol_context='Pending append_notify EntryId, assigned accepted boundary and ballot',trigger='AppendNotify creates Pending; local append or remote Assigned establishes assignment',implementation_guards=['Local acceptance requires self as promised leader in Accept phase.','Pending cap bounds owned requests.','Batch tracking discards stale-ballot intents during reconciliation.'],writes=['Immediate append records accepted_after and current promise; remote Assigned records the supplied index and ballot by EntryId; pending retains oneshot completion sender and deadline.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-notify-assignment'],source_ids=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-assign','M-runtime-loop'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Correlates an application entry to accepted log position whose decision will complete the call.','A2':'Records assignment ballot for supersession checks when authority changes.'},unknowns=['Does completion correctly distinguish an old assigned entry from a replacement at the same decided index?'])\nb2=dict(id='B-runtime-completion',primary_activity='A7',execution_owner='ActorState::drain_notifiers in tick branch',protocol_context='Pending assigned index and current underlying log/promise',trigger='Runtime tick after core tick, event detection, undispatched dispatch and batch reconciliation',reads=['Current decided index, current promise, Pending assignment and deadline.'],important_branches=['Assigned idx <= decided sends Ok(idx) without comparing assignment ballot.','Only otherwise, assignment ballot below current promise sends Superseded.','Only otherwise, expired deadline sends Timeout; remaining pending calls retained.'],external_effects=['Oneshot completion of append_notify.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-notify-assignment','F-decided','F-promise'],source_ids=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-loop','M-runtime-handle','M-runtime-errors'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Turns a log decision boundary into a success response for a particular submitted entry.','A2':'Ballot supersession is evaluated after the decision-boundary branch.'},unknowns=['Can an authentic higher-ballot log replacement and decision arrive between notifier ticks, causing old-entry success?'])\nm['behaviors'] += [b1,b2]\nm['facts'].append(dict(id='F-notify-assignment',meaning='An owned pending EntryId has been associated with an accepted log boundary and ballot by a local append/reconciliation or an Assigned message; this association alone does not establish decision or continued entry identity after a ballot change.',identity={'operation':'EntryId of one pending append_notify','owner':'origin actor'},validity_context='Pending lifetime with the recorded assignment ballot; downstream completion uses current core state.',representation=['Pending.assigned Option<(usize,Ballot)>','Pending.id','Pending.reply'],durability='Volatile actor bookkeeping; not persisted with the core log.',recovery='Actor reconstruction does not restore pending notification futures; core recovery can replace undecided suffix while an actor remains running.',source_ids=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-assign','M-runtime-loop'],unknowns=['Whether the success branch preserves entry identity across higher-ballot suffix replacement.']))\nfor a in m['activities']:\n if a['class_id']=='A7':\n  a['realization_summary']='Actor assigns EntryId operations to accepted boundaries and ballots; tick drains completion by decided index before supersession. Caller owns transport; handle APIs await oneshot results. Subscription and shutdown details remain partly unread.'\n  a['source_ids']+=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-assign','M-runtime-loop','M-runtime-handle','M-runtime-errors'];a['unknowns']=['Success correlation across a replaced undecided suffix is under investigation.','Subscription fan-out and shutdown/backpressure continuation remain partly unread.']\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-sync':\n  b['unknowns']=[]\n  b['important_branches'].append('When incoming decided index exceeds local stored length, Delta base construction reads an incomplete interval; MemoryStorage returns empty before incoming Delta is merged. This condition is distinct from Complete replacement and from full-range reads.')\nfor s in m['surfaces']:\n if s['entry_point']=='InternalStorage::sync_log Delta branch':s['reason']='Conditional incomplete-local-range mechanism is understood; scoped executed answer remains in Candidate and CheckRun records.'\n if s['entry_point']=='omnipaxos_runtime::spawn_actor':\n  s.update(disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B-runtime-assignment','B-runtime-completion'],reason='Assignment and tick completion paths are mapped; subscriber/backpressure and shutdown variants remain open.',source_ids=['M-runtime','M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-assign','M-runtime-loop'])\nm['core_overview']['open_details']=[x for x in m['core_overview']['open_details'] if not x.startswith('Delta snapshot')]\nm['core_overview']['open_details'].append('Async entry completion consumes decided boundaries after recording assignment ballot; replacement across authority change is the next discriminator.')\nchanges={}\nfor id in ['B-sync','core_overview','A7','surface:InternalStorage::sync_log Delta branch','surface:omnipaxos_runtime::spawn_actor']:\n changes[id]=dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['M-sync','M-memory','M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-assign','M-runtime-loop'],rationale='Retain the answered snapshot mechanism and refine runtime navigation from actual consumers; new independent assignment knowledge is added.',preserves='C-delta-prefix and its fixed inputs, requirement, dependencies and observation scope remain unchanged. The new runtime question does not use snapshot recovery as its premise.')\n# A new consumer of existing facts is a dependency change, preserving the prior snapshot proposition.\nchanges['F-decided']=dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-loop'],rationale='Add the newly read runtime notifier consumer of the current decided boundary.',preserves='The existing snapshot obligation checks reconstructed content after recovery, unaffected by this independent runtime consumer.')\nchanges['F-promise']=dict(impact='dependency',source_ids=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-loop'],rationale='Add the newly read runtime consumer of current promise for supersession.',preserves='No promise meaning or existing snapshot check history changes.')\nq=dict(question='Can append_notify return success for an old-ballot entry when a different entry becomes decided at its assigned index before the next notifier tick?',importance='False successful write notification can cause an application to acknowledge a write that is absent from the decided log, despite core consensus remaining safe.',source_ids=['M-runtime-notify','M-runtime-assign','M-runtime-loop','M-runtime-handle','M-runtime-errors','M-log-contract','M-sync','M-leader'],participants=['Origin runtime actor and pending caller','New leader and quorum peer'],objects=['Pending EntryId assignment','Accepted index and ballot','Decided replacement entry'],contexts=['Non-Byzantine same-configuration leadership change','Old entry accepted only locally and not chosen','Higher-ballot synchronization/decision before notifier tick'],event_paths=['append_notify -> append_tracked/record_assignment -> higher Prepare/AcceptSync replaces unchosen suffix -> decided boundary advances -> tick/drain_notifiers'],activity_classes=['A7','A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B-runtime-assignment','B-runtime-completion'],fact_ids=['F-notify-assignment'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-accept':'Determines whether the original or replacement entry was quorum accepted and decided.','B-promise':'Changes authority and excludes old-ballot acceptance.','B-sync':'Can legally replace an unchosen suffix under the new ballot.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Runtime stores assignment ballot and has explicit Superseded handling.','If a notifier tick sees the higher ballot before replacement decision, it returns Superseded rather than success.','A higher ballot can legitimately preserve the original entry; ballot mismatch alone does not prove false success.'],unknowns=['Can a fixed public-API history get a replacement decided before the old pending notifier is drained?','Need correlate the actual completed operation to its original contents and read the completed assigned position; index advance alone is insufficient.'],trigger_rationale='The success branch Some((idx,_)) if idx <= decided precedes the explicit ballot supersession branch. Contract append_notify promises the submitted entry decision; construct a real competing-leader history rather than infer defect from branch order.',disposition='concrete_suspicion',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\ns=dict(action='continue',rationale='Register the independent runtime completion question after the scoped snapshot counterexample was confirmed; update answered source knowledge at this related map handoff.',sources=sources,map_path='runtime_map.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['4fcecc7255ae497e877cff1da4db063b','f628591758414257938b7e7c8d4e0615','B-sync','M-sync','M-memory','M-runtime-notify'],answered='The retained CheckRun and accepted review confirm Delta recovery exposes [22] instead of [11,22] for the missing-interval history. The source relationship now records why the local base is empty. Separately, runtime notifier consumption checks decided index before assignment ballot, yielding a new identity-preservation question.',remaining=['Construct and execute a legal old-entry replacement history for runtime notification.','Do not rerun the already answered snapshot missing-interval scenario.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Different responsibility and principal Fact; the prior snapshot result is retained without being transferred to runtime completion.'))\nopen('runtime_map.json','w').write(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\\\\n');open('runtime_candidate.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python runtime_candidate_build.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\